WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.050
- But it's been 16 years
since "High School Musical".

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.980
Do you remember the beginning of that?

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.180
'Cause that was your
big first thing, right?

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.872
- Yeah. Like I remember all the auditions,

00:00:08.872 --> 00:00:10.190
definitely, 'cause there
were a lot of them.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.270
- Oh really?
- Uh huh.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:12.103
- Oh.

00:00:12.103 --> 00:00:13.830
- Yeah. I mean there were like three,

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.693
but like, I remember them distinctly.

00:00:15.693 --> 00:00:17.230
- You did the same thing with "Idol."

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.087
People don't know that,

00:00:18.087 --> 00:00:19.250
but there were many auditions

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.530
before even got to the TV part.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:21.710
- Oh yeah, of course.

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.440
I like remember meeting
Zac for the first time,

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.286
meeting Lucas for the first time.

00:00:26.286 --> 00:00:27.119
- [Kelly] Oh wow.

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:28.700
- Me and Ashley had already met

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.150
'cause we did a commercial together

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.860
like a month prior.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:32.693
- [Kelly] Random.

00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:33.526
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:33.526 --> 00:00:35.060
- But it's wild.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.130
The time just keeps flying.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.730
- Yeah. Well you start so young.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.000
That's I think that's
what happens when you-

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.140
- Yeah. I'm like I got
decades under my belt now.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.130
- Know it feels weird.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.950
I feel weird saying like 20 years,

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:45.797
that feels weird for me too.

00:00:45.797 --> 00:00:46.630
- Yeah.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.130
- But do you ever hear
from like younger kids

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:48.970
just now discovering it?

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:50.790
Because speaking of my daughter,

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.030
my kids actually were introduced.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.410
My nanny is in love with you as well.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:54.910
So she's showed them "High School Musical"

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:55.743
and they love it.

00:00:55.743 --> 00:00:57.460
So do you have like little
kids now coming back?

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.400
'Cause you're like, that
was a long time ago.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.670
- I mean-
- But they're just seeing it.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.787
- A long time ago.
- I know what they think.

00:01:02.787 --> 00:01:03.620
Is it weird?

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.400
'Cause my daughter, like she'll see people

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.270
and she'll be wait, but
is that the same girl?

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.180
'Cause they don't get that
it came out like years ago.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:10.100
- Totally.
- Do you get kids-

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.740
- I mean, I feel like I
kind of look the same.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.943
- You look, congratulations on that.

00:01:14.943 --> 00:01:15.776
(audience cheers)

00:01:15.776 --> 00:01:17.170
That doesn't work-
- Good genes. Good genes

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.081
- For all of us. Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:19.081 --> 00:01:20.740
- But yeah, like it's so crazy

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.954
because it continues to live
on like for generations.

00:01:23.954 --> 00:01:24.840
- Yeah.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:25.949
- But like that's-

00:01:25.949 --> 00:01:26.782
- Especially with streaming things.

00:01:26.782 --> 00:01:28.890
- That's like the magic
of musicals, though.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:29.723
You know?

00:01:29.723 --> 00:01:32.070
Like I remember watching "West Side Story"

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.590
for the first time when I
was like three years old.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:35.448
- Yeah.

00:01:35.448 --> 00:01:36.640
- And like now there's a new
one for the new generation.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.130
Like musicals, just have
this like legacy about them.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.910
They don't go outta style.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.270
- I think also it has a lot to do,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.110
I mean the story yes,

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:46.910
but also the music is what captivates you

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.500
and I know you put out albums

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.333
while you were doing that.

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:50.970
So are you gonna do that again?

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.000
I like you singing.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.803
- Thank you. I like singing, too.

00:01:53.803 --> 00:01:54.636
(audience cheers)

00:01:54.636 --> 00:01:56.024
They like me singing.

00:01:56.024 --> 00:01:56.857
- Yeah.

00:01:57.924 --> 00:02:00.940
- I definitely had to
sit back for a second

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:04.273
and like figure out what
it is that I wanted to do.

00:02:04.273 --> 00:02:05.106
- Focus on?

00:02:05.106 --> 00:02:08.520
- Yeah. And like, I felt like
if I was gonna do it again,

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.740
I wanted it to be like
really authentically myself

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.830
and like really be my own voice

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.920
and perspective and writing.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.370
And I just like, honestly,
haven't gotten there.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:20.650
It hasn't been like the main priority.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.850
I feel like if I was to do anything,

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.152
like a jazz something
would probably be the first

00:02:25.152 --> 00:02:25.985
to come.

00:02:25.985 --> 00:02:27.429
- That's cool. I love when people do that.

00:02:27.429 --> 00:02:28.262
- I love Jazz.
- Me too.

00:02:28.262 --> 00:02:31.090
But I love when people do
unexpected like that, too.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.880
- Yeah. I mean, it's just personal.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.050
Like that's what I listen to.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.901
Like I've always got Julie
London or Billie Holiday playing

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:39.350
at my house and people
are like, "Interesting."

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:40.620
I'm like, "I'm a grandma. I don't know."

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.540
- Yeah.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.820
I have some grandma tastes about me too,

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:44.624
but I think it's just called good taste.

00:02:44.624 --> 00:02:45.560
- Yes, it is.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.440
- Yeah. I think it's
just like classic sound

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.740
that sounds good-
- Yeah.

